    {
      "id": 71885,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-01T07:26:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So if it's all simultaneous, do you just pick which one to consider \"first\"?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's not simulatenous, nothing in Sentinels is simultaneous. What you have is an attack that hits x targets, you pick the order that those targets are hit in. So for the damage bonus pick which target you wish to hit first and that damage gets the bonus, everything else gets the 'standard' damage.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
